MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_001: Oh my goodness! Now that's a daring rendezvous.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_002: I know it's impolite, but I wish I could see\nmore... Eee!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_003: Oh, Tialla. It's just you over here.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_004: Ludia? Ah!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_005: Oh! I'm not peeping! That would be rude! I would\nnever do that.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_006: No need to explain. Trust me, I've been here a few\ntimes myself.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_007: You like that boy too, don't you, Tialla? You can be\nhonest with me. 
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_008: What?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_009: Hold on. What's this about? I don't even know that\nperson's name.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_010: Ugh! Passing glances, missed connections. How\nromantic, falling in love with a stranger!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_011: No, no, it's not like that! I wanted to see what'd\nhappen when they met up. I know that sounds bad.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_012: But it's not because I liked anyone.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_013: Oh, really? Aww, and just when I thought we were\nheartbreak buddies...
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_014: Heartbreak? What are you saying?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_015: He's an employee of Vandahl Trading. He takes care\nof the horses that transport our goods.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_016: He's a musician at heart and sometimes even sings\nto the horses. Oh, and just look at that face.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_017: Quiet! They'll hear you! They'll see us!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_018: No, they're too wrapped up in each other to see us.\nBesides, he only ever talks about his relationship...
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_019: Nothing I can do about it now. Doubt he even knows\nI exist.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_020: Maybe you should have told him how you feel.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_021: I read about a gifted intellectual whose king dreamed\nup a plan to get her a prestigious appointment.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_022: But at the same time, she got an impassioned plea\nfrom another country and decided to work for them.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_023: So what I'm saying is maybe both prompt action and\npassion play important roles when it comes to love.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_024: I...I think I get it! Wow, Tialla, you're good at this.\nI should have come to you earlier!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_025: Me?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_026: Well, yeah! You pulled that story out of nowhere, and\nit's exactly the advice I needed.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_027: With a friend like you, my love life could actually be\na success!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_028: Let's talk a little later. I'll be leaving my heart in your\ncapable hands!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_C_029: But I don't actually know anything about love.\nI've only read about it in books.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_001: Tialla! Can you believe it? I took your advice, and\nhe actually remembered my name this time!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_002: I'm glad it went well. It was such a simple ploy I was\nworried it wouldn't work.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_003: Simple but effective! So now that he knows who\nI am, what should I do for step two?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_004: Uhh... Well... Finding common ground can really help\nwhen it comes to conversation. Or so I've heard.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_005: And... Umm... Maybe some nice...nail art...would\ndraw his attention?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_006: That's genius! What kind d'you think?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_007: Wh-what kind?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_008: I could do a nice floral pattern...or something even\nmore extravagant.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_009: I bet if anyone knows what I should go with, it's you!\nSo...any suggestions?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_010: Ah, uhm... It... It's... I'm so sorry!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_011: Huh? You OK? Ah, I'm putting too much pressure\non you, aren't I?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_012: The truth is I don't know much about love.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_013: All my tips are just things I read in ancient books.\nI don't have any personal experience to back it up.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_014: I don't think I can help you, Ludia. I'm sorry.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_015: No, I'm sorry. Whether it's from your actual life or \njust a book, you've helped me so much!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_016: There's this author I like, Dante. Her tales are directly\ninspired by real-world research, but...
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_017: There's this author I liked, Dante. Her tales were\ndirectly inspired by real-world research, but...
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_018: Stories written from pure imagination can have just\nas much of an impact!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_019: You really think so?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_020: Your stories were great, Tialla. I owe you one for\nsharing them with me.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_021: Thank you. That's nice to hear.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_022: Good! Just promise you'll tell me more, OK?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_023: I've still got a love life to work on, after all! Not to\nmention, they're pretty inspiring.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_024: Oh? Do you write?
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_025: Eh, sorta. Wouldn't say it's all that great though.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_026: I'm sure that's not true. Storytelling is a noble art.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_027: And I'd love to read anything you've written. I am so,\nso curious.
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_028: You keep that stellar advice coming, and it's a deal!
MID_SE_Tia_Lou_B_029: I'm happy to try!